WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.576
The takeaway: you no longer have to assume
Gaussian, stationary noise.

00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:11.760
By learning the real noise distribution with a
diffusion model and coupling it to a differentiable waveform,

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.084
SLIC produces an unbiased likelihood straight from
detector data.

00:00:16.164 --> 00:00:21.007
This proof of concept, currently single-detector
and four-second segments,

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.936
points toward fast, scalable,

00:00:23.016 --> 00:00:27.060
unbiased inference for future gravitational-wave
observations.
